  "description": "Quantize floating point tensors into 8-bit floating point range [-fp8_max, fp8_max] with local per-block absolute maximum scaling.\n\nBlock-wise FP8 scaling bounds outlier error propagation to small local groups, preserving LLM model accuracy.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\ns_b = \\frac{\\max_{x \\in B} |x|}{x_{\\max}^{\\text{fp8}}}, \\quad q = \\operatorname{clip}\\left(\\operatorname{round}\\left(\\frac{x}{s_b}\\right), -x_{\\max}^{\\text{fp8}}, x_{\\max}^{\\text{fp8}}\\right)\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Partition tensor into localized blocks of size block_size\n2. Compute scale s_b from local absolute block maximum\n3. Scale each block into FP8 dynamic range with saturation clipping\n\n### Returns\nDictionary with 'quantized_tensor' and 'block_scales'.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Implement Block-Wise FP8 Quantization\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nRunning large AI models in production requires massive computing power. During text generation, memory bandwidth (fetching weights and past key-value caches from VRAM) is often the primary bottleneck rather than raw arithmetic compute. **Implement Block-Wise FP8 Quantization** optimizes hardware efficiency, memory consumption, or request serving throughput.\n\nBlock-wise FP8 scaling bounds outlier error propagation to small local groups, preserving LLM model accuracy. In this problem, the goal is to: quantize floating point tensors into 8-bit floating point range [-fp8_max, fp8_max] with local per-block absolute maximum scaling.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\ns_b = \\frac{\\max_{x \\in B} |x|}{x_{\\max}^{\\text{fp8}}}, \\quad q = \\operatorname{clip}\\left(\\operatorname{round}\\left(\\frac{x}{s_b}\\right), -x_{\\max}^{\\text{fp8}}, x_{\\max}^{\\text{fp8}}\\right)\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Partition tensor into localized blocks of size block_size\n2. **Phase 2**: Compute scale s_b from local absolute block maximum\n3. **Phase 3**: Scale each block into FP8 dynamic range with saturation clipping\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Memory Bandwidth Bottleneck**: Quantizing weights to INT8 or INT4 cuts memory traffic in half or quarters, dramatically increasing token generation speeds.\n* **Serving Systems**: Dynamic batching and PagedAttention maximize GPU utilization by grouping requests arriving at different times.\n* **Latency vs. Throughput**: In production serving, systems engineers balance Time-To-First-Token (TTFT) against overall tokens-per-second throughput.",
